From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: restrict TCR2 to long-descriptor contexts

The MSM8226 BSP uses TTBCR only for its short-descriptor contexts.
The upstream MSM8974 short-descriptor proposal likewise programs TCR2
only on the LPAE path. Avoid writing this absent register on MSM8226.

After the shared TZ table initialization was restored, a bounded
userspace configuration snapshot faults precisely at CB0+0x10, while
SCTLR/ACTLR and the actual TTBR/TCR registers remain accessible.
Hardware address translation is now valid after patch0097, so the
unsupported access is unnecessary rather than a candidate fix for
the remaining DSI video failure.

Link: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/iommu/msm_iommu-v1.c
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260809-msm8974-iommu-upstream-v1-4-87f5cd492560@oss.qualcomm.com

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index d037585cc..25e5f299d 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -334,7 +334,8 @@ static int qcom_iommu_program_ctx(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu,
 	iommu_writeq(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_TTBR1, 0);
 
 	/* TCR */
-	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_TCR2, ctx->tcr[1]);
+	if (!qcom_iommu->short_desc)
+		iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_TCR2, ctx->tcr[1]);
 	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_TCR, ctx->tcr[0]);
 	if (qcom_iommu->short_desc)
 		iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_CONTEXTIDR, ctx->pt_asid);
